## @core/string

A string value in JSON can either be a simple string, a number representing UTF-8 code points, or a Unicode escape sequence:

| Value | Description |
|-------|-------------|
| `'foo'` | Simple string |
| `'\u1234'` | Unicode escape sequence |
| `"\\u1234"` | Escaped Unicode escape sequence |
| `"\\\" \\n \t \"` | Escaped Unicode escape sequences |

### @core/string: simple strings

Simple strings are valid JSON strings except they do not contain any escaped characters.

#### Valid

```json
"example"
"\u1234abcd"
"abc\\def\u0001ghi"
"\\u1234\\udcbf\u1234\udcbf"
```

#### Invalid

```json
"example\n"
"example\t"
`"example"`
`\u1234abc`
```

### @core/string: UTF-8 code points

UTF-8 code points can only start with `\u` followed by four hexadecimal digits:

#### Valid

```json
"\u1234"
"\u0000"
"\U00012345"
"\u0000abc"
"\uD800ab"
"\uFFFF"
```

#### Invalid

```json
"\u0000    [1e6, 1e6, 1e6],
    [1e6, 1e6, 1e6]
