# Numeric Edge Cases Test Suite for Python

This test suite is designed to be run against the `python` implementation of the standard library's [`decimal`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/decimal.html) module.

It tests a number of string and integer boundaries that are not represented as literal values in the specification:

* The lowest and highest safe integers (and floats)
* Various edge cases with long or very small numbers, including infinities
* Upper and lower bounds on floating point precision loss
* A variety of special floating-point values
* The maximum number of significant digits allowed by the decimal module
* Various corner cases involving scientific notation
* Different types of arrays: empty, single-element, multi-element, nested, etc.
* Array objects whose keys are numbers of gi* Values that cause overflow when used in arithmetic operations.
* Certain boundary conditions on comparison operators.

## Usage

The test suite itself can be run using `pytest`. It will also generate an HTML report containing the results from each test case.

### Install

```sh
pip install pytest
To run the test suite:

```sh
pytest numeric_edge_cases.py --cov=decimal
